From 646567db2e8dac5373734d41065ec53ae78da286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:37:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-301 lever 4: fuse the qwen4exp QSA mask chain into the
 Vulkan FA

build_attn_qsa materializes a full [n_kv, n_tps] f16 mask per QSA layer per ubatch: fill -inf,
fill zeros, set_rows 0 at the top_k cells, add kq_mask; the sparse FA then reads it again to
compact the finite cells. Vulkan now matches FILL..FLASH_ATTN_EXT (qsa_mask_fa_pattern) and runs
one kernel (flash_attn_qsa_mask.comp) that builds a per-row bitmap of the top_k indices in shared
memory and compacts the selected cells whose kq_mask is finite. It emits the same ascending index
list, so the FA math is unchanged. A dense FA (KV below the sparse floor) gets the mask written by
the same kernel into the ADD node's buffer instead. Graph side: top_k is expanded before the mask
chain so the pattern nodes are consecutive (node order only).
GGML_ARIFI_QSA_MASKFUSE=0 keeps the chain unfused; =red drops the first 64 top_k entries of every
row (planted RED for the op test). New op test QSA_MASK_FA builds the chain node for node as qwen4exp.

Origin: lane-301
Measured-effect: prefill +0.2/+0.9/+0.4/+0.8% at 2K/8K/16K/32K, decode tie (-0.7..0.0%), greedy ids identical 128/128 at every length, served ABBA x2 vs integ 88081ccb8c (cache/qsa-x1-lane/cells/c19-10080535-state.json); op RED FAIL 7/7 (cells/c18-10072033-ops-red.out.log); mechanism RGP compaction dispatch ~42 -> ~18 us at 32K (cells/c18-rgp-*)
